WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.943
- I was a drug dealer,
and I got incarcerated.

00:00:07.157 --> 00:00:09.980
When I came out, I was like
there's no way I'm gonna

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.323
get a second chance or get a job.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.040
I'm trying to achieve and running

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.383
is part of my way of getting there.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.632
- [Narrator] This Great Big
Story was made possible by

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:27.473
Dignity Health. Hello, humankindness.

00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:34.779
(soft piano music)

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.190
- My name is Manuel Navarro, and I am

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.560
a runner with Back On My Feet.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.934
Back On My Feet is an organization

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:53.560
that helps people fight homelessness;

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.404
and at this point in my life,

00:00:55.404 --> 00:00:58.100
the lowest point in my
life, that's where I'm at;

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.210
and it's helping me be successful

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.993
and achieve everything I
wanna achieve the right way.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.940
- My name is Pete Roller,
and I'm a volunteer

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.840
and board member with Back On My Feet.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.260
Manny and I have been running
together for nine months.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.963
We run three mornings a
week at 5:45 in the morning.

00:01:14.963 --> 00:01:17.020
Back On My Feet is a national non-profit

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.310
that works with individuals who are

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:22.603
experiencing homelessness
or in some stage of recovery

00:01:22.603 --> 00:01:25.570
and provides a hand up
to employment and housing

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:28.203
and independence through
community and fitness.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.150
Running is a really nice complement

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.800
to recovery for many of our members.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.560
Running, in particular,
provides the physical release.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:45.240
For a lot of us, we're
replacing negativity.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.512
Those three mornings a
week are the three mornings

00:01:47.512 --> 00:01:50.070
where they know they can
come and be supported

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:51.960
by the rest of the group
and really feel good

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.700
about themselves because
whatever comes in between that

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.690
is gonna be much harder;
and Back On My Feet provides

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:01.220
the link for them to successfully
continue that recovery.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.370
I know it works because the changes

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:07.400
in the individuals,
members, volunteers, myself

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.032
are visible, and they're tangible.

00:02:09.032 --> 00:02:12.630
For our members, it allows
them to feel human again,

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:16.880
and I've seen countless
members just blossom.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.358
When they come to the morning circle,

00:02:18.358 --> 00:02:20.530
they're just another runner.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:21.363
- [Volunteer In Black] Who are we?

00:02:21.363 --> 00:02:22.416
- [Group] Back On My Feet.

00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:23.249
- Where we from?

00:02:23.249 --> 00:02:24.683
- [Group] San Francisco.

00:02:24.683 --> 00:02:25.866
- How far we gonna run?

00:02:25.866 --> 00:02:27.366
- [Group] Forever.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.580
- I hated running, but now I love running.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.960
I mean, just the community;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.120
they make you feel very welcome.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.436
They're really there to help you,

00:02:36.436 --> 00:02:39.920
to embrace you and to
support the fact that

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.757
you're trying to be successful in life

00:02:41.757 --> 00:02:43.490
and trying to do something right.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:47.840
And the connection that me
and Pete have is amazing.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.552
I never had real friends before.

00:02:49.552 --> 00:02:52.270
In the drug business
you don't trust anybody,

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.070
and here I am trusting.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.129
He's always telling me
how I could do better

00:02:57.129 --> 00:02:59.920
and pushing me to do
better and that's good

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.630
because he's there to support me,

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.128
and I think we all
deserve a second chance,

00:03:04.128 --> 00:03:05.629
and I'm taking it.

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:08.379
(intense music)

